  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal and delta Management visitors programme transport costs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal and delta management challenges in Ghana are not addressed through a coherent, integrated approach. Various government agencies are responsible to sectoral aspects only. Institutional mechanisms to coordinate planning and management are lacking. Emergencies like flooding and erosion are dealt with in an ad hoc manner. Likewise, private investments in the area are hampered by this lack of institutional coordination.A visitors programme for (government) stakeholders with regard to delta/coastal management is organised with the following aims:&#x2022;	Putting Ghana on the agenda in the Netherlands as Delta country ,to deepen the links and contacts for possible cooperation and commercial interests;&#x2022;	Taking the first steps toward an institutional framework and integrated approach for coastal and delta management in Ghana (by getting to a common understanding regarding delta challenges in Ghana, insight in relevant best practices in the Netherlands and worldwide).</narrative>
  </description>
